From 0881e9f9ccddb7cf7788540d09c627fe7fb2d021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:18:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The chest keeps its loot, and the obsidian staff stands like
 a person

Two from the play list.

BARROWS. "attacked from another monster, it then closed the interface" and the
reward was gone. Being attacked closes the modal, the [if_close] queued a flush,
and the flush banked everything - so a monster could decide where your loot
went. Worse, INV_MOVEITEM drops the overflow ON THE FLOOR when the destination
is full (InvOps.ts, World.addObj with a 200-tick despawn), which turns a full
bank plus an interruption into Barrows loot lying in a crypt while something is
hitting you. And the chest then said it had nothing of interest, because
%barrows_chest_paid was already true.

Closing the window now does nothing but stop the transmit. The chest keeps what
it paid - barrows_reward_store is scope=perm - and searching it again hands it
straight back through a new ~barrows_chest_reopen, which transmits and opens and
does not roll. The flush survives in exactly one place, immediately before a NEW
chest rolls, so the window still only ever shows one chest's payout and a run
abandoned entirely is still banked the next time you dig in.

OBSIDIAN STAFF. "broken animation and stance": the Toktz-mej-tal carried
thzaar_staff_ready and thzaar_staff_walk, which are the animations a TZHAAR
wielding a staff uses, on a human skeleton. 32 of the 33 weapon_staff objs use
human_staffready and NOT ONE of them overrides the walk, because a one-handed
staff walks the way the player walks. It now does both. Its attack and defend
were already the human_stafforb pair 23 other staves use and are untouched.

Also: 14 of barrows_mutate's labels named the value the MUTATION makes true
rather than the wording of the check that catches it - "ahrim is combat 99" for
a check that says 98 - so "caught by its own check" could never fire for any of
them. mutate_labels is down from 14 unmatched to 1 across the tree.

Two checks of mine went in wrong first. The new "flush in exactly one place"
check duplicated an older "emptied BEFORE a new chest rolls" one, so a mutation
to the flush could only ever be attributed to one of them - the blanket-on-top-
of-precise fault the TzHaar round found. And four staff mutations anchored on a
run of params 23 other staves share, so replace(..., 1) edited a different staff
and the obby-specific checks stayed green - the Magic Dart fault again.

barrows_battery and combat_battery ALL PASS, 21 chest and staff mutations each
caught by its own check, rs2check 0 ERROR 0 CHECK, selftest PASS, eleven
batteries ALL PASS. Not compiled: npm is still 403ing zod.

